    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 77.19 score stands as the slate's elite play. His matchup against Marte provides a significant SP skill advantage (+19%), allowing him to comfortably lead our starters in projected efficiency. Close behind is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** at 74.56; while we are waiting on the official card, his projected #4 spot paired with a +14% platoon edge against Pfaadt makes him a high-leverage target. **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson** also present strong plays (66.71 and 65.81, respectively), benefitting significantly from a 16% park boost and the aggressive \"slow delivery\" factor against Gasser, which optimizes their stolen base upside\u2014a critical priority for our roster strategy.\n\nThe decision to keep **Nasim Nunez** on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. His score of 54.17 reflects a robust 13% SP skill advantage against McGreevy, but he was ultimately edged out by the superior power-profile scoring of **Josh Jung** and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Nasim Nunez** offers categorical versatility, the optimizer prioritized the higher cumulative R/RBI potential of the starting group. Conversely, we are tracking the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** closely; both are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and any significant drop in the batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to our bench depth. We remain cautious with **Liam Hicks**, whose 48.98 score sits near our floor; he is active primarily for his platoon edge, but he remains a candidate for mid-game substitution should his first two plate appearances prove stagnant.",
